From 974a3719b76d6c4a8c77c0c01ce5532ad0e2bdbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:42:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Desktop link protocol 2 on the page's side: a probe of
 three fields, the host's info in the welcome, RemoteVersionError

detectHost returns a RemoteHostProbe (app, protocol, requiresCode) and no longer says the host's name, cores or Node version before the
code; the welcome carries them and connectRemote hands them back as RemoteConnection.info (RemoteHostInfo, protocol 2). connectRemote
takes an optional probe (no request of its own), and a host of another version of the link gives a RemoteVersionError with both numbers,
from the probe, from the welcome or from the host's 4426 close. wire.ts holds the shared link constants (the version, the close codes, the
sentence of a scenario that is too big).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016zPE7K49ycKieo7wJdrBFN
