From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:59:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] Desktop host: the throttled-link measurement tool, the
 real-browser checks, the container's memory limit, README for the 0.9.0 flags

linkMeasure.ts and link.mjs run the real host as a process with a simulated link in front of it and record the host's memory, the time to the
first picture, the round trip of a ping, an explain and a pause under load, and what the run took. e2e/host-browser.spec.ts is the real-browser
check of the Host allowlist (Chromium's --host-resolver-rules maps a hostile name to 127.0.0.1) and of the one-use link of --open. The default of
--max-session-mib counts on the container's limit when it is lower than the computer's memory. The README documents every flag, the apps and
other origins, IPv6, --open, the memory bound with its measurements and the engine link of protocol 2.

